OL,3,GNEWSAWWI soldier identified after more
OL,4,Athan a century
OL,5,
OL,6,FFor 108 years, the grave of a World War
OL,7,FOne solider who died in battle sat in a
OL,8,FFrench cemetery, unidentified.
OL,10,FAll that was known was that the man was
OL,11,Fpart of the King's Shropshire Light
OL,12,FInfantry, who were fighting in the
OL,13,FSomme region, and died in March 1918.
OL,15,FHe was originally buried in a plot with
OL,16,Fdozens of other unknown British
OL,17,Fsoldiers within the German cemetery at
OL,18,FGrevillers. In 1920, 34 bodies were
OL,19,Fexhumed from the plot to be identified
OL,20,F- of those, four remained unnamed, one
OL,21,Fwith the rank of corporal.
OL,23,APub: 18-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBC Eng (W) NewsCReg TVFWeather
FL,358,350,200,160,0,100
